WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.012
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:09.675
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:16.528
Unit fifteen: Insurance Industry. Today you will state conditions with unless, provided that and as long as.

4
00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:19.388
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:23.613
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.776
Policy premium.

7
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:30.954
Policy premium means the amount paid regularly for insurance cover.

8
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.724
The policy premium is paid monthly.

9
00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:37.538
Your turn. Say: Policy premium.

10
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.738
Policy premium.

11
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:43.705
Risk assessment.

12
00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:48.806
Risk assessment means the process of judging how likely a loss is.

13
00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:51.834
A risk assessment decides the price.

14
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.752
Your turn. Say: Risk assessment.

15
00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.845
Risk assessment.

16
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:02.002
Claim process.

17
00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:07.036
Claim process means the steps for asking an insurer to pay for a loss.

18
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.091
The claim process takes about two weeks.

19
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:13.672
Your turn. Say: Claim process.

20
00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:17.952
Claim process.

21
00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:19.764
Underwriting.

22
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.106
Underwriting means evaluating risk to decide whether to offer insurance.

23
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:28.099
Underwriting rejected the risky applicant.

24
00:01:28.683 --> 00:01:31.127
Your turn. Say: Underwriting.

25
00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:34.979
Underwriting.

26
00:01:35.717 --> 00:01:36.729
Deductible.

27
00:01:37.717 --> 00:01:41.551
Deductible means the amount you pay yourself before insurance pays.

28
00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.428
A higher deductible lowers the premium.

29
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:47.588
Your turn. Say: Deductible.

30
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:51.655
Deductible.

31
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:53.615
Coverage limit.

32
00:01:54.617 --> 00:01:58.602
Coverage limit means the maximum amount an insurer will pay.

33
00:01:59.217 --> 00:02:01.808
The coverage limit was ten thousand dollars.

34
00:02:02.417 --> 00:02:05.255
Your turn. Say: Coverage limit.

35
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.298
Coverage limit.

36
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.098
Actuary.

37
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:16.521
Actuary means an expert who calculates risk and insurance costs.

38
00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:19.929
An actuary studies accident statistics.

39
00:02:20.517 --> 00:02:23.273
Your turn. Say: Actuary.

40
00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.192
Actuary.

41
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.392
Insurance fraud.

42
00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:34.542
Insurance fraud means lying to an insurer to get money you do not deserve.

43
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.067
Insurance fraud raises premiums for everyone.

44
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:41.429
Your turn. Say: Insurance fraud.

45
00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.150
Insurance fraud.

46
00:02:46.967 --> 00:02:50.792
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:57.913
Visal, my policy says 'The insurer will pay provided that you report the loss within a week.' What does 'provided that' mean?

48
00:02:59.017 --> 00:03:07.068
It means 'only if'. Provided that, as long as and on condition that set a condition for something to happen.

49
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:09.568
And 'unless'?

50
00:03:10.683 --> 00:03:18.644
Unless means 'if not'. 'Unless you pay the premium, your cover will end.' We do not add a second negative.

51
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.877
So the claim process has conditions?

52
00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:33.112
Always. As long as the damage is within the coverage limit and there is no insurance fraud, the claim will be paid after the deductible.

53
00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:35.976
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:36.817 --> 00:03:40.929
Grammar focus: Conditions: unless and provided that and as long as.

55
00:03:41.229 --> 00:03:42.521
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:43.217 --> 00:03:46.400
The insurer will pay provided that you report the loss within a week.

57
00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:49.885
Your cover will end unless you pay the premium.

58
00:03:50.783 --> 00:03:54.176
A claim is paid as long as it is within the coverage limit.

59
00:03:55.133 --> 00:04:02.418
Unless = if not, so never add a negative: 'unless you pay', not 'unless you don't pay'. Provided that and as long as mean 'only if'.

60
00:04:03.183 --> 00:04:07.159
Be careful! Don't say: Unless you don't pay, cover ends.

61
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.052
Say: Unless you pay, cover ends.

62
00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.223
Unless already means 'if not'.

63
00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:17.604
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.715
Reading the Small Print.

65
00:04:20.015 --> 00:04:23.895
An insurance policy is a promise that depends on conditions.

66
00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:30.383
An insurer will pay a claim provided that the loss is reported quickly and falls within the coverage limit.

67
00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:34.608
Unless you pay the policy premium, the cover will end.

68
00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:40.699
Underwriting and risk assessment decide the price, as long as the information given is honest.

69
00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.313
Insurance fraud, however, makes honest customers pay more.

70
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.216
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.421
Your cover will end blank you pay the premium.

72
00:04:53.721 --> 00:04:57.398
A, unless. B, if not. C, provided.

73
00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.968
The answer is A: unless.

74
00:05:04.117 --> 00:05:07.649
The maximum amount an insurer will pay is the blank limit.

75
00:05:07.949 --> 00:05:11.637
A, coverage. B, premium. C, claim.

76
00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.049
The answer is A: coverage.

77
00:05:18.183 --> 00:05:20.938
An expert who calculates risk is an blank.

78
00:05:21.238 --> 00:05:25.599
A, actuary. B, underwriter's deductible. C, agent.

79
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:31.156
The answer is A: actuary.

80
00:05:32.317 --> 00:05:34.026
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:34.326 --> 00:05:40.777
A, Unless you don't pay, cover ends.. B, Unless you pay, cover ends.. C, Unless pay you, cover ends..

82
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.331
The answer is B: Unless you pay, cover ends..

83
00:05:48.483 --> 00:05:51.830
According to the reading, fraud makes honest customers pay…

84
00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:55.353
A, more. B, less. C, nothing.

85
00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.493
The answer is A: more.

86
00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:04.898
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:10.501
Why do insurance companies employ actuaries to study statistics and risk?

88
00:06:19.317 --> 00:06:20.863
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:21.163 --> 00:06:48.469
Insurance companies employ actuaries because prices must match the real chance of loss. If premiums are too low, the company loses money; if they are too high, customers go elsewhere. Actuaries use statistics on accidents, illness and disasters to calculate fair premiums. As long as the calculations are accurate, both customers and insurers are protected.

90
00:06:48.769 --> 00:06:50.455
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:57.636
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and conditions: unless and provided that and as long as.

92
00:06:57.936 --> 00:07:02.330
Today's value is analytical thinking. Look for the pattern underneath the surface.

93
00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.642
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:05.942 --> 00:07:08.908
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

